<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gansu Corridor</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hexi Corridor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a> Corridor, also called the Hexi Corridor, is a narrow strip of land in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> between mountains and desert, linking China with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a>'s seizure of it from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu Empire</a> deprived them of valuable grazing lands and opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gansu-corridor.jpg" alt="Gansu Corridor" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Han Lei · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Linze,_Zhangye,_Gansu,_China_-_panoramio_(4).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
